    > dential/95%-sample/h4_dataset.dta saved

.         
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H4 * 
. 
.         *  Analogously to H1 analysis, we regress the gender equality  index 
.         * (GE_index) [0,1] onto the indicator of having at least one daughter
>  in 
.         * 2018 and a group of control variables. Additionally, to control for
>  group 
.         * effect heterogeneity, we include an interaction term of daughter in
> dicator
.         * and the gender of the parent. 
.         
.         * thus, we run a linear OLS regression analysis with GE_index as depe
> ndent
.         * variable. here as well, we also control for missing values of contr
> ol
.         * variables. 
. 
.         * The coefficient estimate of interaction term 1.d_daughter#1.female 
> is of 
.         * main interest.
.         
.         * We use robust standard errors. 
.         
.         reg GE_index i.d_daughter##i.female c.age i.mig i.educ i.east   i.mar
> rital_stat  i.polit i.religiosity, r

